{"nota":"Diccionario ES→EN. El inglés se genera con tools\\i18n.ps1 generar; no editar el .en.js a mano. keep: textos que no se traducen.","lit":{"\u0027 (fermentación láctica)\u0027":"\" (lactic fermentation)\"","\u0027 · ATP neto \u0027":"\" · net ATP \"","\u0027 · consumo de O₂ \u0027":"\" · O₂ consumption \"","\u0027 · sin O₂\u0027":"\" · no O₂\"","\u0027 ATP por glucosa\u0027":"\" ATP per glucose\"","\u0027/glucosa\u0027":"\u0027/glucose\u0027","\u0027\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e1 · Coenzimas reducidas (condiciones aerobias)\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e1 · Reduced coenzymes (aerobic conditions)\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e3 · Termodinámica\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/table\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e3 · Thermodynamics\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eBalance por molécula de glucosa · \u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eBalance per glucose molecule · \"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eAerobio: \u003cb\u003e≈ 32 ATP por glucosa\u003c/b\u003e (2,5 ATP/NADH y 1,5 ATP/FADH₂). Anaerobio: solo \u003cb\u003e2 ATP\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eRotenona\u003c/b\u003e bloquea CI; \u003cb\u003ecianuro\u003c/b\u003e bloquea CIV; \u003cb\u003eoligomicina\u003c/b\u003e bloquea la ATP sintasa; el \u003cb\u003eDNP\u003c/b\u003e disipa el gradiente (\u003cb\u003edesacoplante\u003c/b\u003e): consume O₂ y libera calor, sin ATP.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eAerobic: \u003cb\u003e≈ 32 ATP per glucose\u003c/b\u003e (2.5 ATP/NADH and 1.5 ATP/FADH₂). Anaerobic: only \u003cb\u003e2 ATP\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eRotenone\u003c/b\u003e blocks CI; \u003cb\u003ecyanide\u003c/b\u003e blocks CIV; \u003cb\u003eoligomycin\u003c/b\u003e blocks ATP synthase; \u003cb\u003eDNP\u003c/b\u003e dissipates the gradient (\u003cb\u003euncoupler\u003c/b\u003e): it consumes O₂ and releases heat, without ATP.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eDiez reacciones: la fase de \u003cb\u003einversión\u003c/b\u003e gasta 2 ATP (hexocinasa, PFK-1); la fase de \u003cb\u003ebeneficio\u003c/b\u003e produce 4 ATP y 2 NADH. \u003cb\u003eRendimiento neto: 2 ATP + 2 NADH\u003c/b\u003e por glucosa. Sin O₂, el piruvato se reduce a \u003cb\u003elactato\u003c/b\u003e para regenerar NAD⁺.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eTen reactions: the \u003cb\u003einvestment\u003c/b\u003e phase spends 2 ATP (hexokinase, PFK-1); the \u003cb\u003epayoff\u003c/b\u003e phase produces 4 ATP and 2 NADH. \u003cb\u003eNet yield: 2 ATP + 2 NADH\u003c/b\u003e per glucose. Without O₂, pyruvate is reduced to \u003cb\u003elactate\u003c/b\u003e to regenerate NAD⁺.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEl acetil-CoA (2 C) se une al \u003cb\u003eoxalacetato\u003c/b\u003e (4 C) y forma \u003cb\u003ecitrato\u003c/b\u003e (6 C). Dos \u003cb\u003edescarboxilaciones\u003c/b\u003e liberan 2 CO₂ y regeneran el oxalacetato. Por vuelta: \u003cb\u003e3 NADH, 1 FADH₂, 1 GTP\u003c/b\u003e; por glucosa, dos vueltas.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eAcetyl-CoA (2 C) joins \u003cb\u003eoxaloacetate\u003c/b\u003e (4 C) and forms \u003cb\u003ecitrate\u003c/b\u003e (6 C). Two \u003cb\u003edecarboxylations\u003c/b\u003e release 2 CO₂ and regenerate oxaloacetate. Per turn: \u003cb\u003e3 NADH, 1 FADH₂, 1 GTP\u003c/b\u003e; per glucose, two turns.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eLa \u003cb\u003eglucosa\u003c/b\u003e se oxida en tres etapas: \u003cb\u003eglucólisis\u003c/b\u003e (citosol), \u003cb\u003edescarboxilación del piruvato y ciclo de Krebs\u003c/b\u003e (matriz mitocondrial) y \u003cb\u003efosforilación oxidativa\u003c/b\u003e (membrana interna). La energía de las oxidaciones queda en \u003cb\u003eNADH y FADH₂\u003c/b\u003e, que alimentan la cadena respiratoria.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eGlucose\u003c/b\u003e is oxidized in three stages: \u003cb\u003eglycolysis\u003c/b\u003e (cytosol), \u003cb\u003epyruvate decarboxylation and the Krebs cycle\u003c/b\u003e (mitochondrial matrix) and \u003cb\u003eoxidative phosphorylation\u003c/b\u003e (inner membrane). The energy of the oxidations is stored in \u003cb\u003eNADH and FADH₂\u003c/b\u003e, which feed the respiratory chain.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eLos electrones del NADH (−0,32 V) caen hasta el O₂ (+0,82 V). \u003cb\u003eCI, CIII y CIV bombean H⁺\u003c/b\u003e al espacio intermembrana, creando el \u003cb\u003egradiente protónico\u003c/b\u003e (Δp). Los H⁺ regresan por la \u003cb\u003eATP sintasa\u003c/b\u003e, cuyo rotor impulsa la síntesis de ATP (\u003cb\u003equimiosmosis\u003c/b\u003e, Mitchell).\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eThe electrons of NADH (−0.32 V) fall down to O₂ (+0.82 V). \u003cb\u003eCI, CIII and CIV pump H⁺\u003c/b\u003e into the intermembrane space, creating the \u003cb\u003eproton gradient\u003c/b\u003e (Δp). The H⁺ return through \u003cb\u003eATP synthase\u003c/b\u003e, whose rotor drives ATP synthesis (\u003cb\u003echemiosmosis\u003c/b\u003e, Mitchell).\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027«Etapa», «Inhibidor», «Oxígeno» (con o sin O₂) y «Avance».\u0027":"\u0027stage, inhibitor, oxygen (with or without O₂) and progress.\u0027","\u00272 acetil-CoA (C₂)\u0027":"\"2 acetyl-CoA (C₂)\"","\u00272 ATP + 2 FADH₂\u0027":"\"2 ATP + 2 FADH₂\"","\u00272 ATP + 2 NADH\u0027":"\"2 ATP + 2 NADH\"","\u00272 piruvato (C₃)\u0027":"\"2 pyruvate (C₃)\"","\u002736 ATP\u0027":"\"36 ATP\"","\u00274 ATP + 4 NADH\u0027":"\"4 ATP + 4 NADH\"","\u0027acetil-CoA (C₂)\u0027":"\"acetyl-CoA (C₂)\"","\u0027Acetil-CoA + 3 NAD⁺ + FAD + GDP → 2 CO₂ + 3 NADH + FADH₂ + GTP\u0027":"\"Acetyl-CoA + 3 NAD⁺ + FAD + GDP → 2 CO₂ + 3 NADH + FADH₂ + GTP\"","\u0027aconitasa\u0027":"\"aconitase\"","\u0027activa el complejo I\u0027":"\"activates complex I\"","\u0027Aerobio\u0027":"\"Aerobic\"","\u0027Aerobio ≈ 32 ATP; fermentación = 2 ATP\u0027":"\"Aerobic ≈ 32 ATP; fermentation = 2 ATP\"","\u0027aldolasa\u0027":"\"aldolase\"","\u0027anillo con carbonos y descarboxilaciones.\u0027":"\"ring with carbons and decarboxylations.\"","\u0027Aplica un desacoplante: sube el consumo de O₂, pero baja el ATP.\u0027":"\u0027Apply an uncoupler: O₂ consumption rises but ATP falls.\u0027","\u0027ATP fosf. oxidativa\u0027":"\"Oxidative phosph. ATP\"","\u0027ATP glucólisis\u0027":"\"Glycolysis ATP\"","\u0027ATP Krebs (GTP)\u0027":"\"Krebs ATP (GTP)\"","\u0027ATP por glucosa según condición\u0027":"\"ATP per glucose by condition\"","\u0027ATP por glucosa según la condición, torre redox de la cadena respiratoria y balance energético de la oxidación de la glucosa.\u0027":"\u0027ATP per glucose by condition, redox tower of the respiratory chain and energy balance of glucose oxidation.\u0027","\u0027ATP sintasa\u0027":"\"ATP synthase\"","\u0027ATP total\u0027":"\"Total ATP\"","\u0027aumenta el gradiente\u0027":"\"increases the gradient\"","\u0027ausente\u0027":"\"absent\"","\u0027Avance\u0027":"\"Progress\"","\u0027Avance automático\u0027":"\"Automatic progress\"","\u0027azul: glucólisis · amarillo: Krebs (GTP) · naranja: fosforilación oxidativa\u0027":"\"blue: glycolysis · yellow: Krebs (GTP) · orange: oxidative phosphorylation\"","\u0027Balance\u0027":"\"Balance\"","\u0027Balance e inhibidores\u0027":"\"Balance and inhibitors\"","\u0027Balance energético de la oxidación de la glucosa\u0027":"\"Energy balance of glucose oxidation\"","\u0027bloquea el canal de H⁺ de la ATP sintasa\u0027":"\"blocks the H⁺ channel of ATP synthase\"","\u0027bloquea la ATP sintasa\u0027":"\"blocks ATP synthase\"","\u0027bomba de H⁺ y ATP sintasa; prueba inhibidores.\u0027":"\"H⁺ pump and ATP synthase; try inhibitors.\"","\u0027C₆H₁₂O₆ + 2 NAD⁺ + 2 ADP + 2 Pᵢ → 2 piruvato + 2 NADH + 2 ATP\u0027":"\"C₆H₁₂O₆ + 2 NAD⁺ + 2 ADP + 2 Pᵢ → 2 pyruvate + 2 NADH + 2 ATP\"","\u0027Cada \u003cb\u003eNADH\u003c/b\u003e rinde ≈ 2,5 ATP y cada \u003cb\u003eFADH₂\u003c/b\u003e ≈ 1,5 ATP.\u0027":"\"Each \u003cb\u003eNADH\u003c/b\u003e yields ≈ 2.5 ATP and each \u003cb\u003eFADH₂\u003c/b\u003e ≈ 1.5 ATP.\"","\u0027Cadena respiratoria\u0027":"\"Respiratory chain\"","\u0027Calor: \u0027":"\"Heat: \"","\u0027carbonos\u0027":"\"carbons\"","\u0027Cianuro\u0027":"\"Cyanide\"","\u0027Cianuro (CIV)\u0027":"\"Cyanide (CIV)\"","\u0027Ciclo de Krebs\u0027":"\"Krebs cycle\"","\u0027cit c\u0027":"\"cyt c\"","\u0027Citrato\u0027":"\"Citrate\"","\u0027citrato sintasa (+acetil-CoA)\u0027":"\"citrate synthase (+acetyl-CoA)\"","\u0027Colores\u0027":"\u0027Colours\u0027","\u0027compara el ATP de cada condición.\u0027":"\"compare the ATP of each condition.\"","\u0027Compara en el gráfico el ATP por glucosa con y sin O₂.\u0027":"\u0027Compare ATP per glucose with and without O₂ on the chart.\u0027","\u0027Complejo I\u0027":"\"Complex I\"","\u0027Complejo IV\u0027":"\"Complex IV\"","\u0027Con O₂\u0027":"\"With O₂\"","\u0027Condición elegida\u0027":"\"Chosen condition\"","\u0027Consumo O₂\u0027":"\"O₂ consumption\"","\u0027Controles\u0027":"\u0027Controls\u0027","\u0027desacopla\u0027":"\"uncouples\"","\u0027detiene el ciclo de Krebs de inmediato\u0027":"\"stops the Krebs cycle immediately\"","\u0027Diana\u0027":"\"Target\"","\u0027diez pasos con ATP neto y NADH.\u0027":"\"ten steps with net ATP and NADH.\"","\u0027disipa el gradiente de H⁺: más O₂ consumido, menos ATP\u0027":"\"dissipates the H⁺ gradient: more O₂ consumed, less ATP\"","\u0027DNP\u0027":"\"DNP\"","\u0027DNP (desacoplante)\u0027":"\"DNP (uncoupler)\"","\u0027E°′ (V): NADH −0,32 → Q +0,04 → cit c +0,25 → O₂ +0,82. CI, CIII y CIV bombean H⁺.\u0027":"\"E°′ (V): NADH −0.32 → Q +0.04 → cyt c +0.25 → O₂ +0.82. CI, CIII and CIV pump H⁺.\"","\u0027Eficiencia 32 × 50 / 2 870\u0027":"\"Efficiency 32 × 50 / 2,870\"","\u0027El aceptor final de electrones de la cadena respiratoria es…\u0027":"\"The final electron acceptor of the respiratory chain is…\"","\u0027El cianuro bloquea…\u0027":"\"Cyanide blocks…\"","\u0027El ciclo de Krebs ocurre en…\u0027":"\"The Krebs cycle takes place in…\"","\u0027el citosol\u0027":"\"the cytosol\"","\u0027el complejo I\u0027":"\"complex I\"","\u0027el complejo IV\u0027":"\"complex IV\"","\u0027El complejo IV reduce ½O₂ a H₂O con 2 H⁺.\u0027":"\"Complex IV reduces ½O₂ to H₂O with 2 H⁺.\"","\u0027el espacio intermembrana\u0027":"\"the intermembrane space\"","\u0027El gradiente se vuelve máximo y frena el bombeo, de modo que cesa el consumo de O₂.\u0027":"\"The gradient becomes maximal and brakes the pumping, so O₂ consumption ceases.\"","\u0027el retículo endoplásmico\u0027":"\"the endoplasmic reticulum\"","\u0027electrones\u0027":"\"electrons\"","\u0027En la cadena respiratoria quita el O₂: la cadena se detiene y la glucólisis regenera NAD⁺ formando lactato.\u0027":"\u0027In the respiratory chain remove O₂: the chain stops and glycolysis regenerates NAD⁺ by forming lactate.\u0027","\u0027energía\u0027":"\"energy\"","\u0027Energía almacenada como ATP: \u0027":"\"Energy stored as ATP: \"","\u0027enolasa\u0027":"\"enolase\"","\u0027Escena y condiciones\u0027":"\"Scene and conditions\"","\u0027espacio intermembrana (H⁺ ↑)\u0027":"\"intermembrane space (H⁺ ↑)\"","\u0027Etapa\u0027":"\"Stage\"","\u0027formar acetil-CoA\u0027":"\"form acetyl-CoA\"","\u0027Fosforilación a nivel de sustrato\u0027":"\"Substrate-level phosphorylation\"","\u0027Frontal\u0027":"\"Front\"","\u0027Fructosa-1,6-bisP\u0027":"\"Fructose-1,6-bisP\"","\u0027Fructosa-6-P\u0027":"\"Fructose-6-P\"","\u0027fumarasa\u0027":"\"fumarase\"","\u0027Fumarato\u0027":"\"Fumarate\"","\u0027General\u0027":"\"General\"","\u0027Glucólisis (azul), GTP de Krebs (amarillo) y fosforilación oxidativa (naranja).\u0027":"\"Glycolysis (blue), Krebs GTP (yellow) and oxidative phosphorylation (orange).\"","\u0027Glucosa\u0027":"\"Glucose\"","\u0027Glucosa (C₆)\u0027":"\"Glucose (C₆)\"","\u0027Glucosa + 6 O₂ → 6 CO₂ + 6 H₂O   (ΔG°′ 